          "kind": "paragraph",
          "text": "Trade Marks Act 1995"
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "text": "Trade Mark Regulations 1995"
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "text": "Oppositions to protection of international trade marks may be based on the grounds contained in sections 39, 41 (177 for certification trade marks), 42, 43, 44, 58, 58A, 59, 60, 61, 62A, and regulations 17A.28(2A) and 17A.34(4) (see reg 17A.34 for the necessary modifications). International trade marks cannot be defensive trade marks, so section 187 does not apply."
        }
      ],
